 # Rotation Alignment Matrix
 ## Overview
-Computes a 3x3 rotation matrix that rotates a source vector to align with a target vector using Rodrigues' rotation formula components [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of orienting geometry or camera views relative to a specific direction, which is a prerequisite for consistent voxelization or spatial hashing in volume rendering pipelines. It differs from [PCA Rotation](4256-pca-rotation.md) by rotating between two arbitrary vectors rather than deriving the rotation from the data's statistical covariance.
